From 6e285a0c39e9c26a949a0fbd244c617a630330c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: esacademy-de <98397027+esacademy-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:08:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] net: phy: dp83867: add ti,led-function to select the LED
 sources

The PHY's four LED outputs (LED_0, LED_1, LED_2 and the GPIO_0 pin as
LED_3) default to link / 1000BT link / RX-TX activity / 100BTX link.
Boards that wire the LEDs differently (for example a Raspberry Pi
style RJ45: green = link with blink on activity, amber = 1000BT link)
need other sources, but the selection is lost on every PHY soft reset,
so it cannot be left to a one-shot userspace write: an "ip link set
down/up" returns the PHY to its defaults.

Add an optional ti,led-function property with the four LEDCR1 source
codes in the order LED_0, LED_1, LED_2, LED_GPIO and re-program LEDCR1
from dp83867_config_init(), after the reset done by phy_init_hw().
Without the property the PHY's default LED configuration is untouched,
and the existing PHY LED class device callbacks keep working.

